{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8GQAp5gzrAVoJqaRjRK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The description asks for one thing: `apply` should reject no-op changes, using two new `ApplyError` variants. These parts of the diff do exactly that and need no capability:\n\n- the `ZeroQuantity` and `AlreadyDiscontinued` variants (lines 36–39);\n- the zero-quantity arm (lines 70–72);\n- the already-discontinued guard (lines 85–87).\n\nThe diff also adds three things the description never mentions:\n\n- **`load_file`** (lines 51–54) is a new public function that takes an `Fs` capability and reads any `path` that capability allows. Before this change the library held no capability at all: `load` parsed bytes, `save` produced bytes, and the caller did the I/O. Now the library contains code that reads files.\n- **`LoadError::Io`** (line 28) and the `fs::Fs, io` import (line 1) exist only to support `load_file`.\n\nNothing about rejecting no-op changes needs filesystem access. So this change gives the library file-reading authority that its description does not call for.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"reject\", \"findings\": [{\"line\": 52, \"item\": \"load_file\", \"authority\": \"fs\", \"what\": \"Adds a new public function that holds an Fs capability, which the library never held before, unrelated to rejecting no-op changes.\"}, {\"line\": 53, \"item\": \"load_file\", \"authority\": \"fs\", \"what\": \"Reads an arbitrary caller-supplied file path through Fs, giving the library file-reading authority the description does not mention.\"}]}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":5837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"dia